From 06d314c322a357a471d8597555964b5fa16f1674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:39:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build/InterpreterStartup: the interpreter's startup kit;
 NDCodeSimulator and NTimeHierarchy re-pointed

A new module below CodeSimulator with eight public lemmas harvested from
NDCodeSimulator's private startup pieces (the header projections and their
capture, a silent capture's first return, the suffix window, the released
install call, the layout call restated over the serialization's pairing, the
seam step) and U2-S's fresh-capture start (embedSilentCfg_initCfg), so that
B5a's uniform simulator can cite them (megafill C's review of the B5a brief,
Q-B1, option A; the user's ruling of 2026-10-24). NDCodeSimulator re-points
its eight privates to the kit; NTimeHierarchy's un_step is the kit's
seamCompTM_step. Statements unchanged; the suffix drop stays a private
helper of the window call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
